AU  - Livacic, Gaston Ernesto Passi
TI  - National Migration Policy of Chile "Sello Migrante"
T2  - Mendeley Data
M3  - Data set
C8  - 2
AB  - The central axis of the following article establishes the analyses and characterization of the evaluate guidelines request by the New Policy in Migration Management of de National Migration Services of Chile to the Township that have been recognized with the certification. For such purposes, all the Townships that have participated in the initiative are evaluated, from its inception in the December 2015 to December 2022, in the cases of revalidated Townships, the evaluation of the last Report sent is considered. The evaluation criteria by the public policy under observation consist of five large dimensions, however, the present proposal focuses its attention on characterizing the emerging institutionalism in local governments in points (I) Institutionally and (II) Training. Indeed, it is intended to analyze the behavior associated with the implementation of an unprecedented public policy in the treatment of current international migration phenomenon, particularly, the type of articulation among themselves the central structure of the State, certified local governments and foreigners residing in those territories. Likewise, observing management difficulties such as the new ideas that have been arise from some Townships to continue deepening (impact) the new migration public management existing in the country.
