AU  - da Cruz Duran, Maria Renata
AU  - de Barros Oliveira Bueno, Belmira Amelia
ED  - Chova, LG
ED  - Martinez, AL
ED  - Torres, IC
TI  - PUBLIC POLICY OF CONTINUING TEACHER TRAINING IN CHILE
T2  - 7TH INTERNATIONAL TECHNOLOGY, EDUCATION AND DEVELOPMENT CONFERENCE (INTED2013)
M3  - Proceedings Paper
CP  - 7th International Technology, Education and Development Conference (INTED)
CL  - Valencia, SPAIN
AB  - Chile currently has a polysemic system of continuous teacher training, as well as a full schedule of goals: standardization of evaluation parameters, definition of common objectives for training, in-depth studies about the characteristics of their demand. Aligned these goals point to old Latin American problems, such as lack of rigor operating within government, the former centrality of operating projects and subsequent gentrification of the public attended. From presentation of this general framework, it is expected to discuss the Chilean Schedule of continuing education teacher for the past 20 years and compare it to Brazil, checking the implications, the existence and scope of common models of teacher education continued in Latin America. We begin by describing the Chilean population scale and the numbers of education. Then, we discuss the design of this State and its implications in teaching trainningat academic and educational reforms. Laws, teacher education programs and funding are put into play to understanding the general sense of public policies of education in the country and its parallel with Brazil.
