TI  - Chile's Economic Integration Policy and the Nation's Industrialization
TI  - 칠레의 산업화에서 경제통합정책의 역할과 효율성에 대한 고찰
T2  - Korean Journal of Latin American and Caribbean Studies
T2  - 중남미연구
M3  - research-article
AB  - Chile, known as the most stable and economically eficient coun try in Latin America, has propelled the regional economic integration policy as the main policy of economic development. This policy was promoted in the 1990s after the civil government was inaugurated in Chile with the ar rival of democratization. The internationalization of Chilean economy wa s something different from the previous military government of Pinochet. However, the industrialization is not fully achieved stil in Chilean econom y as the mineral commodities, mostly copper, account for more than half of the chilean export. There is somewhat more to do with respect to the industrializat ion of chilean economy. The actual economic model of Chile has come to the top of it's role. Chile needs to overcome the current RIA model and look for the new development model for the industrialization.
