TY  - JOUR
AU  - Fuentes Vera, Cristian
TI  - The Chilean Transition's foreign policy from its internal sources
T2  - SI SOMOS AMERICANOS-REVISTA DE ESTUDIOS TRANSFRONTERIZOS
M3  - Article
AB  - The foreign policy of the Chilean Transition (to democracy) is considered a successful example of international reintegration, in the context of Chile being a small country, far from the centers of world power and politically isolated due to seventeen years of dictatorship. However, it seems wrong to separate foreign policy from domestic policy, as it is a formal distinction that disregards the importance of regime change in the decision making process, a process determined by internal sources such as the characteristics of the transition, the self-perception that Chile has about its role in the world, its economic model, the role of the Presidency of the Republic, the influence of the Armed Forces, and the country's diplomatic tradition.
