AB  - The monetary policy framework being used in Chile has permitted the country to attain and maintain a low and predictable inflation, improve its capacity to accommodate external shocks, and contribute to the creation of a macro environment that is favorable to economic growth. This policy framework, combined with a market-oriented economy and the improved external conditions, permitted a growth rate of 6.1% in 2004, as well as positive prospects for coming years, while significantly reducing output variability.
