TY  - JOUR
AU  - Brambilla, Emma Minerva
TI  - Policy, Waste, and Power: Textile Dumping in Chile's Atacama Desert
T2  - LATIN AMERICAN POLICY
M3  - Article
AB  - Globally, 87% of textile fibers end up incinerated or in landfills, with Chile bearing the brunt of this crisis. Every year, 39,000 tons of discarded clothing are illegally dumped in the Atacama Desert, turning it into a sacrifice zone for the Global North's waste economy. In response, Chile introduced the "National Solid Waste Policy 2018-2030" to regulate textile waste, yet its gaps perpetuate rather than resolve environmental injustice and existing power relations. This research addresses the question, how does the "National Solid Waste Policy 2018-2030" contribute to the reproduction of existing power relations in the Atacama Desert? Applying Lukes' three-dimensional power framework, this research argues the policy excludes marginalized communities (first dimension), shields Global North actors from accountability (second dimension), and depoliticizes textile dumping as a technical issue (third dimension). To break this cycle, urgent preventive measures-including Extended Producer Responsibility laws, trade reforms, and the formalization of informal waste workers-must be implemented before 2030. Still, prevention alone is insufficient. This research advances a bold restoration strategy, inspired by ocean cleanup initiatives, to convert textile waste into renewable biofuels.(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic), 87%(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic), (sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic).(sic)(sic), (sic)3.9(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic), (sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic).(sic)(sic), (sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)"2018-2030(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)"(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic), (sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic), (sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic).(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)"2018-2030(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)"(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)?(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)Lukes(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic), (sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic) ((sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)), (sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic) ((sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)), (sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic), (sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic) ((sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)) .(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic), (sic)(sic)(sic)2030(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic), (sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic),(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic).(sic)(sic), (sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic).(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic), (sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic), (sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic).A nivel mundial, el 87% de las fibras textiles terminan incineradas o en vertederos, siendo Chile quien carga con el peso de esta crisis. Cada a & ntilde;o, 39.000 toneladas de ropa desechada son vertidas ilegalmente en el desierto de Atacama, transform & aacute;ndolo en una zona de sacrificio para la econom & iacute;a de residuos del Norte Global. En respuesta, Chile introdujo la "Pol & iacute;tica Nacional de Residuos S & oacute;lidos 2018-2030" para regular los residuos textiles; sin embargo, sus deficiencias perpet & uacute;an -en lugar de resolver-la injusticia ambiental y las relaciones de poder existentes. Esta investigaci & oacute;n aborda la siguiente interrogante: & iquest;c & oacute;mo contribuye la "Pol & iacute;tica Nacional de Residuos S & oacute;lidos 2018-2030" a la reproducci & oacute;n de las relaciones de poder existentes en el desierto de Atacama? Aplicando el marco tridimensional del poder de Lukes, este estudio argumenta que dicha pol & iacute;tica excluye a las comunidades marginadas (primera dimensi & oacute;n), exime de rendici & oacute;n de cuentas a los actores del Norte Global (segunda dimensi & oacute;n) y despolitiza el vertido de textiles al tratarlo como una cuesti & oacute;n meramente t & eacute;cnica (tercera dimensi & oacute;n). Para romper este ciclo, deben implementarse medidas preventivas urgentes-incluyendo leyes de Responsabilidad Extendida del Productor, reformas comerciales y la formalizaci & oacute;n de los trabajadores informales de residuos-antes del a & ntilde;o 2030. No obstante, la prevenci & oacute;n por s & iacute; sola resulta insuficiente. Esta investigaci & oacute;n propone una audaz estrategia de restauraci & oacute;n-inspirada en las iniciativas de limpieza oce & aacute;nica- destinada a transformar los residuos textiles en biocombustibles renovables.
