TY  - JOUR
AU  - Sepulveda, Paulo Cesar Sepulveda
TI  - The importance of sustainability approach for marine resources policy-making in Chile
T2  - MARINE POLICY
M3  - Article
AB  - Despite being one of the top 10 countries in the world regarding fishing capture, Chile is facing important issues in relation to the sustainability of its fisheries. Considering this scenario, this work, in the first place, analyses the situation of fishing sustainability from the conceptual level in the relevant Chilean legal instruments, noting that the fishing legislation established an atrophied sustainability concept. This conclusion arrives noting that sustainability aims at understanding the human-environment condition and interactions with the objective of meeting the needs of society while sustaining the life support systems of the planet. However, this environmental dimension was omitted. Nevertheless, the silenced aspect of sustainability can be restored from a factual standpoint using the conceptual foundations derived from environmental law and the right framework for sustainable policymaking in the fishing arena. Therefore, through a case study that shows how sustainability is operationalized in the energy sector, several virtuous consequences are derived. The framework analyzed in this case study is strategic environmental assessment, which has been barely utilized despite its benefits. Hence, the main conclusions of this work refer to the importance of making a national fishing policy in Chile, constructed with the mentioned framework, to obtain a navigation chart for the whole sector, produced with a systemic, precautionary, anticipatory, and democratic approach.
