TY  - JOUR
AU  - Jara, Ignacio
AU  - Claro, Magdalena
TI  - The ICT policy for schools in Chile (red links): Digital Skills Assessment
T2  - CAMPUS VIRTUALES
M3  - Article
AB  - In the context of the ICT policy for schools named Enlaces Network propelled for 20 years by the Chilean state, a first evaluation of digital skills (SIMCE TIC) was applied in 2011 to a national simple of students. This paper presents Enlaces' policy and analyzes the foundations and results of this first measurement. The SIMCE TIC measured the technological and cognitive abilities to manage information, interact with others and behave in an ethical way in the digital world. These skills were evaluated through software that simulates the virtual environment of a computer and productivity, communication and navigation tools to solve problems posed to students. Approximately half the students evaluated in the SIMCE TIC achieved only the initial level of performance in the test, showing Enlaces policy's limitations to develop these skills in students. These results also confirm the novelty and complexity that these skills represent for the Chilean educational system and open an informed discussion related to the challenges and difficulties that the ICT policy must face in this area in the future.
