AU  - Brito-Doerr, Marisol
TI  - Halfa century of Housing Policy in Santiago de Chile: State Action and Residencial Segregation
T2  - CIUDAD Y TERRITORIO-ESTUDIOS TERRITORIALES-CYTET
M3  - Article
AB  - The article examines nearly half a century of Chilean housing policy (1978-2024) and its socio-spatial impact on the Metropolitan Region of Santiago, filling a gap in the literature by providing a long-term temporal analysis that combines the study of housing regulations with the socio-spatial evolution of subsidized housing. From a historical perspective, it analyzes the continuities and transformations of housing programs, as well as the locational trends of subsidized housing in relation to the metropolitan structure. The analysis is based on five dimensions: target population, form of tenure, financing, actors involved, and production and spatial distribution. The results show the persistence of a neoliberal logic that has reinforced segregation and territorial inequalities in Santiago.
