TI  - From Indians to Citizens: Indigenous Policy, Negotiation and Adjustment in Chile (1818-c. 1860)
T2  - ANUARIO DE ESTUDIOS AMERICANOS
M3  - Article
AB  - This article examines the relation between the nascent Chilean republic and the former indios or indigenous from the monarchic period, through the study of two regions: the Chiloe province and the central zone of Chile. From the study of both cases, we will identify: 1) the legal and extralegal mechanisms used for the citizenization of the indios, and 2) the negotiation and adjustment developed by those indigenous in the new political context, with the double result of the ladinizaci??n and the practice of an indigenous citizenship.
