TY  - JOUR
AU  - Mehendale, Smita
TI  - Impact of FDI Retail Policy on Domestic Organized Retailers – A Comparative Analysis with China, Germany and Chile
M3  - Article
AB  - The Indian Retail sector has tremendous growth potential. It is already one of the largest contributors to GDP and employs more than 8% of the work force in India. However, the current Indian FDI policy in retail has earned more flack from within the country than from foreign retailers due to its potential threat to the unorganized and existing organized retail in India. Several emerging economies have gone through the same phase much before and today are reaping the benefits of a modern retail sector. India is still lagging behind in reforms in this sector. This paper aims to examine the threats of FDI in retail to the existing organized retail in India as against its benefits by drawing comparisons with the experiences of other economies like China, Germany and Chile.
