AU  - Sposito, Italo Beltrao
TI  - Actors and structures in Argentina and Chile for an assessment of foreign policy changes after ideological transitions.
T2  - RELACIONES INTERNACIONALES
M3  - Article
AB  - This article comparatively analyzes how domestic variables influence foreign policy changes in Argentina and Chile following presidential successions involving ideological shifts (Kirchner-Macri, 2015; Bachelet-Pinera, 2010). Using a Most Similar System Design, it argues that presidential decision-making centralization, autonomy of specialized bureaucracies, and political system structure determine the stability of foreign policy after ideological changes in leadership. It concludes that Argentina's strong presidentialism led to greater foreign policy changes compared to Chile's more institutionalized presidentialism, contributing to debates on domestic and institutional conditions influencing Latin American foreign policy stability and continuity.
